<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  ============================================================================
  CURATED CATALOG FEED : the real products the live site sells
  ============================================================================
  (XML comments may not contain a double hyphen, so dividers use '=' below.)

  NOT the same thing as local_catalog_feed.xml next to it. That file is a
  deliberately MESSY fixture with placeholder images, written to exercise the
  parser's error paths, and its truth table is asserted by tests. THIS file is
  clean production data: every item is a garment the site actually offers, with
  the name, brand and AED price the owner set, and a photo that really exists
  under public/dev-catalog/.

  It exists because the partner network (Admitad MENA / Impact / ArabyAds) is
  still in moderation, so there is no live FEED_URL to import from. Until there
  is, the catalog is curated by hand and shipped in git, and it reaches an
  environment through the real import pipeline:

      php artisan catalog:import-file

  (and its "file" option points the same command at any other XML file, which
  is spelled with two hyphens that an XML comment is not allowed to contain.)

  That command runs the REAL ImportFeedJob (XmlFeedParser to brand filter to
  upsert), so nothing here takes a shortcut past production code. The upsert
  keys on external_id and touches ONLY the items listed below, which is why the
  curated products live in their own file: importing the messy dev fixture into
  a live catalog would rewrite unrelated rows.

  ============================================================================
  BRAND ALLOW-LIST
  ============================================================================
  ImportFeedJob drops any brand missing from feed.brands (FEED_BRANDS in .env).
  Every brand below must be listed there or the item is silently filtered:
  OneByOne, Zimmermann.

  ============================================================================
  IMAGE URLS ARE ABSOLUTE, ON PURPOSE
  ============================================================================
  image_flat_url is handed straight to FASHN as the garment image
  (GenerateLookJob, GenerateOutfitJob) and FASHN fetches it over the internet.
  A site-relative "/dev-catalog/x.jpg" is unreachable from there, so these point
  at the public origin that serves public/dev-catalog/. Change the host here if
  the site ever moves; nothing derives it at runtime, because a feed is external
  data and does not get to read our config.

  ============================================================================
  A NOTE ON flat_bg_verified
  ============================================================================
  Import always lands products unverified (the automatic verifier is a stub), so
  they stay out of GET /api/catalog until a human publishes them:

      php artisan catalog:verify EXTERNAL-ID ...

  Five of the seven dresses below are photographed as the garment alone on
  white, which is what public/dev-catalog/README.md asks for and what the try-on
  engine can dress. Two are photographed ON A MODEL: both Zimmermann items. The
  site owner decided on 2026-09-07 to publish those anyway; the trade-off is
  recorded in that README, not hidden here. (ONEBYONE-DRESS-MIDI-WHITE-LACE was
  on a model too until 2026-11-03, when the shop's own garment-alone shot
  replaced it.)
-->

